18. A sample of hydrogen gas is collected in a partially water-filled eudiometer tube at a temperature of 27°C and a total pressure of 745 mm Hg. If the volume of the hydrogen gas collected in the eudiometer tube is 47 mL, determine the number of moles of the hydrogen gas. The water vapor pressure is calculated using the following equation, where "x" is the temperature in °C.
Vapor pressure (mm Hg) = 5.901×e^{0.0506x}
(Note: The given text is already partially translated, so the translation is applied only to the Bangla portions, and the rest remains unchanged.)
